{"scenario":"sis-flow-off-discard-rejected","rows":["S-0019","S-0022","S-0023","S-0028","S-0163","S-0027","A-0105","A-0107","A-0108","A-0109","A-0110","A-0111","S-0161","B-0279","C-0019","C-0020","C-1050"],"source":"Ed4 S.4.1, p.S-5","description":"A client whose unfinished U_PDUs reach eight MTUs is sent S_DATA_FLOW_OFF; what it sends next is discarded, with reason 13 for one that asked for confirmation; when the count falls to four MTUs it is sent S_DATA_FLOW_ON and its U_PDUs are accepted again.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","csma":{"mode":"jitter"},"modem":{"preamble_ms":600,"flush_ms":150,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":256,"block_ms":4800}]}},"note":"The external busy input holds the channel busy from 0 (P5-4), so the MAC stays in SENSE and nothing goes on air (K-0066). Conn 1 binds SAP 5 for non-ARQ (service type tx_mode 2, no confirmation) and gets S_BIND_ACCEPTED with MTU 2048 (A-0041, A-0047); flow is on with no S_DATA_FLOW_ON (interp S-0027). At 0 it sends eight S_UNIDATA_REQUESTs to SAP 5 at 0.0.1.3, DELIVERY MODE default, TTL 30 (60000 ms, A-0089), each a 2048-byte U_PDU (bytes i, i\u002B1, ... mod 256 for the i-th, i from 0). Each is accepted and goes to the DTS at once (A-0189); the first starts dts.ttd at its TTD (C-1050), the rest share that TTD. Under interp S-0163 every accepted U_PDU counts against its client until the lower sublayers are finished with it, and the eighth brings conn 1 to 16384 bytes, eight MTUs, so the node sends S_DATA_FLOW_OFF (type 16, interp S-0111) after accepting it (S-0019, S-0022). At 1000 conn 1 sends \u0027ping\u0027 with DELIVERY MODE ARQ and node delivery confirmation (Transmission Mode 1, Delivery Confirmation 1): it passes the over-MTU, delivery mode and broadcast checks (S-0161), so it is discarded because flow is off and, having asked for confirmation, rejected with S_UNIDATA_REQUEST_REJECTED reason 13, Data Buffers Full, echoing SAP 5, 0.0.1.3 and the U_PDU (S-0023, A-0107, A-0109 to A-0111; interp S-0028); no soft link is asked for. A non-ARQ \u0027lost\u0027 at 1000 with no confirmation is discarded silently. At 60000 dts.ttd expires and the DTS rejects all eight C_PDUs for TTL (C-1050); the timer is not running, so nothing is cancelled. Each rejection reaches the SIS through the CAS and ends that U_PDU\u0027s count; after the fourth, conn 1 is at 8192 bytes, four MTUs, and gets S_DATA_FLOW_ON (S-0021; interp S-0163). None asked for confirmation, so no S_UNIDATA_REQUEST_REJECTED. At 61000 \u0027again\u0027 (TTL 30) is accepted again: dts.ttd starts for it."}
